from scene import H,ROOT,load
def main():
 phase=load('results/phase_summary.json');stable=load('results/stability.json');idle=load('results/idle.json');cost=load('results/cost_summary.json');clear=load('results/clearance.json');hw=load('results/hardware.json');motion=load('results/motion.json');audit=load('results/delivery_audit.json');park=load('results/park_search.json');reach=load('results/reachability.json')
 iterations=[load(str(p.relative_to(H))) for p in sorted((H/'results/iterations').glob('M??.json'))]
 rows='\n'.join(f'| {r["config"]["trial"]} | {r["config"]["mount_height"]:.2f} / {r["config"].get("mount_tilt_deg",0)}° | {r["clear_samples"]}/3 | {len(r["audit"]["packing_hits"])} | {r["config"]["change"]} |' for r in iterations)
 phases='\n'.join(f'| {r["name"]} | {r["static_ok"]} | {r["internal_ok"]} | '+('; '.join('/'.join(x['pair']) for x in r['dominant_rejections'][:2]) or 'none')+' |' for r in phase['rows'])
 clr='\n'.join(f'| {cat} | {r["samples"]} | {r["min_reserve_mm"]:.3f} | {r["p05_reserve_mm"]:.3f} | {r["fraction_at_least10mm"]:.1%} |' for cat,r in clear['categories'].items())
 extra='\n'.join(f'| {r["mount_height_m"]:.2f} | {r["target"]} | {r["ok"]} | {r["counts"]} |' for r in reach['extra_design_probes'])
 text=f'''中文摘要：本轮在独立目录重建了小范围有线移动底盘方案，完成 **{len(iterations)} 轮结构迭代**，采用台前工作的单 UR5e、固定 **850 mm／20°倾角**安装面、**660 × 500 mm** 四轮驱动底盘和 **46.6 kg** 低位配重；模型整机质量 **{hw['cart']['total_model_mass_kg']:.3f} kg**，不装电池或升降轴。电源经柜脚防护线槽进入小车，卷线器和短线段包络均已纳入设计；实际卷线自动控制及轮毂制动连接仍未完成机械资格验证。

胡萝卜 **{phase['strokes_pass']}/11 个完整局部动作**通过，即曼陀林切片行程和提起退离；端点独立通过不能当作连续制作。实际执行连接 **0/10**、成品 **0/4**，完整停放 **fail**。停放快照在假设的台面右端空位中通过，柜门／烤箱门扫掠边界间距 **{park['door_sweep_separation_m']*1000:.1f} mm**，但照片没有证明这个空位存在。

最终复核的已接受候选、局部路径与停放状态中，最小抗倾覆距离余量 **{stable['min_tip_margin_mm']:.3f} mm**，已计入运动臂／负载重力、加工力、加速度和拉线作用的 1.5 动态系数。该数字不是整餐执行证明。保留原始 **0.57 kg** 食物状态，未提交任何制作事件。备菜时间 **null**；含一次 15% 预备费和一次 18,000 元家庭安全包的预算为 **{cost['total_cny']:,.2f} 元**。本轮按停止条件 **(b)** 交付；没有采购、联系供应商或实物试验。

**Outcome and authority.** This is a failed carrot-first feasibility delivery, not a released robot design or a proof that a mobile kitchen robot cannot work. The binding authority is [DECISIONS.md](../../DECISIONS.md), including the R09 replacement of the wall rail and the short/fixed-height preference. [Package and reproduction](../../sim/r09/integrator/README.md), [iteration ledger](../../sim/r09/integrator/results/iterations.csv), [delivery audit](../../sim/r09/integrator/results/delivery_audit.json). The T08 result demonstrates that a different front-working mobile machine passed sixteen independent phases; it does not transfer that machine's geometry, brakes, torque or connected execution to this cobot.

**Hardware choice.** Three combinations use the same tethered cart: FAIRINO FR5, DOBOT CR5 and UR5e. FR5 is the preferred cost-down candidate (5 kg, 922 mm, about 22 kg), but its advertised CNY 18,000 FR5-SPARK price was a restricted 2023 education programme, not a general current quote. Its model, mounting-specific envelope and power-loss behaviour were not qualified here. The working allowance is CNY 45,000. [OEM offer](https://fairino.com/Companynews/37.html), [FR5 specification](https://www.fairino.us/collaborative-robot/fairino/fr5). CR5 has 5 kg payload, 900 mm reach and 25 kg body mass; CNY 90,000 is an unquoted allowance. [DOBOT specifications](https://www.dobot.cn/products/cr-series/dobot-cr-series.html?lang=cn).

UR5e was selected as the numerical baseline because complete inherited geometry and the rated-CoM basis were available. It has 5 kg payload, 850 mm reach, 20.6 kg catalogue mass, and 570 W maximum power. The complete model inertias, rather than the catalogue total, drive the stability calculation. The historical China procurement reference is **CNY 140,000 arm + 30,000 controller + 10,000 pendant**. It must not be reported as a 140,000-yuan complete system or a 2026 quotation. [UR datasheet](https://www.universal-robots.com/media/1807465/ur5e_e-series_datasheets_web.pdf), [CSU procurement](https://czzx.csu.edu.cn/csustatic/zbgshwfwl/20221213/3497.html). There is no finding that a cheaper arm fails the envelope; comparison qualification remains incomplete. The FR5/CR5 allowance-based total alternatives are CNY {cost['alternative_FR_allowance_total_cny']:,.0f} / {cost['alternative_CR_allowance_total_cny']:,.0f}.

The drive is four ZLTECH ZLLG65ASM500 V2.0 powered wheels: 48 V, 165 mm nominal diameter, 129.5 mm full axial envelope, 4.85 kg each and 10 Nm rated torque. The selected scene includes the housing and inward spindle, with tolerance allowance, not just the narrow tyre. M01–M08 used preliminary wheel proxies; M09 onward is the sourced full drive geometry. At 0.10 m/s the nominal wheel speed is about 11.6 rpm. Dry level-floor rolling resistance 0.03, 0.15 m/s² acceleration and a 20 N tether allowance give about 79 N total drive-force demand, or about 1.6 Nm per wheel assuming equal sharing. These are sizing assumptions, not traction tests. [OEM drawing](https://www.zlingkj.com/Data/zlingkj/upload/file/20240102/ZLLG65ASM500%20V2.0%E5%8D%95%E5%87%BA%E8%BD%B4.pdf). Four-point floor contact, motor loss, skid scrub and mounting compliance remain installation assumptions.

Mayr ROBA-stop M spring-applied 8 Nm brakes are a sourced brake family, but **the wheel motor spindle is stationary**. A separate rotating-hub-to-brake coupling and its full envelope still need CAD and proof. No built-in wheel brake is inferred from the wheel datasheet. [Mayr brake](https://www.mayr.com/en/products/safety-brakes/industrial-brakes/roba-stop-m~55). The 18 kg chassis budget includes the brake carriers. The secured ballast is 25 mm total steel plate thickness in a 50 mm protective envelope. Brake and force assumptions prevent this concept from receiving hardware release even where statics passes.

The EOAT selection is DH PGC-140-50: 138.5 × 75 × 75 mm housing, 1 kg body, 50 mm stroke, self-locking, and 40–140 N per jaw. Its full housing was added to the inherited fingers and wider palm. The binding checker still uses total normal force 150 N, μ=0.5, SF=1.5 and 150 N/15 Nm keys. The final checker additionally enforces the OEM 7 Nm moment allowance and 50 mm total jaw stroke; the complete keyed adapter and load path remain qualification work. [DH product catalogue](https://www.dh-robotics.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/DH-Robotics-Servo-Electric-Grippers-Product-Gallery-202203D.pdf).

**Mount height, localization and layout.** The upright base-joint gravity envelope is exactly zero: a vertical-axis joint experiences no gravity torque from the rated payload. Under the binding gravity-derived envelope rule, horizontal process demands therefore fail that denominator. A fixed 20° mount gives a nonzero base-axis envelope; no guessed motor torque was substituted. Both 0° and 20° envelopes were recomputed using two numerical restarts per joint and feasible OEM self-clear witnesses. These are conservative sampled maxima, not global-optimum proofs. [Envelope](../../sim/r09/integrator/assets/envelope_20.json).

The selected fixed mount is 850 mm. No lift is added because the observed blockers are fixture/food/gripper interference and ownership transitions, not evidence that vertical travel resolves the tasks. Base x/y/yaw is sampled at every start and frozen for each stroke. The planned docking accuracy is ±2 mm XY, ±0.2° yaw and ±1 mm height, using hard stops plus fiducials and applied wheel brakes. XY plus yaw at 850 mm reach already consumes about 5 mm before hand-eye error and compliance; this is a design requirement, not a measured positioning guarantee. Extra geometry reserve does not itself prove the 5 mm TCP pose tolerance under those errors.

The user photos were inspected. They show an L kitchen with a crowded sink/prep leg and hood on the hob leg. The simulation retains the R08 standard kitchen solids, sink, closed upper leaves and protected hob region as a conservative reference arrangement; it is not a dimensionally reconstructed digital twin of the photographed kitchen. Appliance clutter must be removed from the assumed prep spaces. The extra right-end alcove x=1.8…2.8 m is explicitly assumed. No unknown ceiling clearance is exploited.

All stations and four full bowls remain present in every carrot model. M11 retains low mandoline, P16 peeler, greens and tomato stations, with an upright 240 mm basket on three real 20 mm pads. Its bottom is at 670 mm; the unchanged wall-spout water axis crosses the opening about 76 mm off-centre, within the 118 mm inner radius. This is a ray/containment observation, not proof of all-surface washing. The GROHE spout and NC valve remain selected. [GROHE](https://www.grohe-mena.com/en_cy/eurocube-bath-spout-13303000.html).

**Eleven structural iterations.** Each row ran three full-scene endpoint probes with 96 actual starts apiece. A green map point is an independent admitted configuration, never a completed stroke. The selected M11 has zero detected cross-station solid intersections. Moving the peeler rearward in M07 produced two fixed-part intersections and was rejected.

| Iteration | Height m / tilt | Clear corridors | Fixed intersections | Change |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
{rows}

Additional empty-gripper design probes test the low sink space, front counter and rear bowl. These are separate from food-task admission; no volumetric workspace completeness is claimed. [Reachability data](../../sim/r09/integrator/results/reachability.json), [map render](../../sim/r09/integrator/renders/reach_map.png).

| Height m | Target | Admitted | 96-start outcomes |
|---|---|---|---|
{extra}

**Carrot result and structural blockers.** All eleven templates received 96 starts at each endpoint, then continuation with a frozen base from admitted starts. Successful full internal paths are limited to the mandoline work stroke and holder retreat. [Phase results](../../sim/r09/integrator/results/phase_summary.json).

| Template | Both independent endpoints | Full local path | Dominant candidate rejection pairs |
|---|---|---|---|
{phases}

The raw tray lacks an under-finger clearance feature for the retained grasp; a physical end cradle is a more appropriate next change than a collision exemption. The peeler corridor still conflicts with complete food, cradle, cutter or guard geometry, even after correcting the 9 mm seating-datum error. It needs a mechanically defined retract/load/seat sequence. The catch tray needs a real detachable support and grasp, followed by a bowl transfer over the complete bail/rim geometry. Current food-holder loading, guard closure, terminal 10 mm stub handling, post-peel rinse and separate scrap disposal also lack checked bindings. No hidden appliance event removes a robot-touched lid, tool or container.

Every adjacent connection was actually searched as enter carry → drive → leave carry, with at least 60 seconds allocated per stage, restarts, staging and shortcut attempts. The saved interstroke searches use the narrow-footprint safe carry pose archived in `results/pilot/upright_carry_search.json`; stage names `fold` and `unfold` refer to entering and leaving that pose. Visual review found that it was not folded sufficiently for idle, so idle was rerun with explicit ≥1.6 rad elbow bending. The final parked render uses this corrected folded pose. Base routes retain the departing held geometry, constrain the arm to a safe carry envelope, check a 4 mm point-displacement bound and reject lateral skid-drive motion. All {len(motion['rows'])} staged links remain unexecuted. Independent optimal base samples need not form a compatible station-to-station chain; this finite search does not establish that every possible common dock assignment fails. [Motion records](../../sim/r09/integrator/results/motion.json).

**Rules and state repair.** The actual R05 source remains unchanged, SHA-256 `{audit['reference_sha256']}`. The adapter retains 5 mm/3° poses, 10 mm robot/environment and arm/arm, 5 mm held/gripper/environment, PAD=0, μ=0.5, SF=1.5 and the keyed limits. It retains native reference contact rejections alongside conservative distance bounds; the R08 native-distance disagreement was not used to override a failure.

Canonical identities now include local quaternion, dimensions, type and attachment-chain transforms. Constructor checks reject forged tray dimensions or orientation; live checks reject changed held/finger identities. Named grasp faces cannot be obtained from a matching name alone. All contact capabilities have an explicit kind and at most 50 mm extent, and working permissions are absent on transfer paths. Four contiguous, station-validated work capabilities span the golden 200 mm mandoline stroke.

`commit_path` rejects supplied Cartesian positions, rebuilds the authoritative scene, checks joint dimensionality/finite values/start continuity, derives food positions from FK, checks every gap/load/stability state and every ≤4 mm step, and requires safe carry for base movement. It rejects incompatible station operations and aggregate slice/scrap overlap transactionally. The synthetic regression now has {len(audit['regression']['tests'])} passing checks, including a valid checked hold and rejected unchecked jump/stale start. Those synthetic tests do not alter the delivery food ledger. [Regression](../../sim/r09/integrator/results/regression.json), [state ledger](../../sim/r09/integrator/results/state_sequence.json).

**Forces and products.** Mandoline geometry is unchanged: 330 × 120 × 60 mm deck, 65 mm radius holder, 80 mm work/CoM offset, 0.55 kg loaded holder and 200 mm stroke. Both lateral signs of (−60, ±10, +20) N are checked; (−40, ±10, +20) N is nominal. The golden file's sensitivity loads are not substituted. Other retained sizing values are P16 peeling 63 N tangential/7.5 N normal, greens 348.8516 N, and tomato 636.3651 N, with their original assumptions and source limitations. They are not measured forces for these custom fixtures. [Unchanged process/source contract](../../sim/r09/integrator/assets/process_contract.json), [primary root-cut study](https://iseki-food-ejournal.com/article/69/pdf).

Potato, bok choy and tomato execution is deferred after carrot failure. Their required 4–6 mm slices with post-cut starch rinses, 30–50 mm greens sections with basal-crease cleaning, and eight tomato wedges remain unchanged. All products retain ≥98% edible delivery, separate bowls and the original quality conditions. No finished product is counted.

**Stability and robustness.** For each audited pose, the code sums gravity and process moments, finds the ground reaction centre, and measures signed distance to the inset support rectangle ±215 × ±175 mm. The final factor 1.5 scales moving-arm/held gravity, process wrench, acceleration and cable disturbance while chassis gravity remains static. The audit covers both process-force signs, horizontal acceleration cases and any horizontal 20 N cable pull at a 100 mm inlet. The minimum audited margin is **{stable['min_tip_margin_mm']:.3f} mm**, with a minimum recorded restoring moment of **{stable['min_restoring_moment_Nm']:.3f} Nm**, across {stable['samples']} saved admitted candidate/local-route/park states. There are zero executed meal states. Four supported tyre contacts, flat floor, restrained ballast and the cable tension cap are conditional requirements. [Stability](../../sim/r09/integrator/results/stability.json).

The final audit also replays all admitted M11 corridor-map candidates and the empty-gripper design probes at the selected 850 mm mount. Rejected poses and alternative-height designs do not become admissions to the selected machine. Clearance reserves below are beyond the binding gates, using the final replay. They are not robustness statistics for an executed meal. Any sub-2 mm entries are enumerated in the JSON; zero self-category reserve can arise at inherited palm/key shoulder geometry and is disclosed rather than relaxed. Nonself near-gate samples are not suitable for design freeze. Neither installation errors nor compliance have been simulated away.

| Category | Samples | Minimum reserve mm | P05 mm | ≥10 mm reserve |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
{clr}

[Clearance data](../../sim/r09/integrator/results/clearance.json). The parked snapshot is clear of the full cabinet/oven sweep boundary by {park['door_sweep_separation_m']*1000:.1f} mm; doors are closed obstacles during motion and sweep obstacles only at idle. Fold/unfold and drive attempts do not close a connected carrot-to-park sequence, so idle remains failed. [Idle](../../sim/r09/integrator/results/idle.json).

**Tether, home safety, power and schedule.** The selected Brennenstuhl 1241000300 reel has 16+2 m cable, H07RN-F 3G1.5, automatic spring rewind, a 480 × 140 × 320 mm case and 6.6 kg stationary mass. Its 230 V rating is **1,000 W coiled**, about 4.35 A, versus 3,500 W fully uncoiled. The 3,500 W figure is not available while unused cable stays wound. The toe guide and shrouded front branch keep a loop out of the main standing aisle; the cable checker uses wheel sweeps and conservative separation from arm/held/kitchen solids. Trip and pinch provisions include the fixed cover, presence inhibition, tension fault stop and intentional restart. [Reel](https://www.brennenstuhl.com/en-DE/products/cable-reels/automatic-cable-reel-ip44-16-2m-h07rn-f-3g1-5).

The reel manual describes a ratchet and cautions high retraction forces. Automatic ratchet release, controlled tracking through the floor guide and the proposed 20 N limit are **not qualified behaviours** of the stock reel. The 924 W cart allowance includes arm, limited drive supply, IPC/sensors and gripper but excludes unverified brake-release coils. It leaves only 76 W coiled-rating headroom; power sizing is therefore not closed. Station appliances use a separate dry fixed power track, with a provisional 500 W budget and no heater. [Hardware/power details](../../sim/r09/integrator/results/hardware.json).

The single CNY 18,000 home safety package includes presence/door pause sensing, E-stop, RCD/PE, leak and cable tension detection, blade interlocks and control. UR joint holding follows the OEM brake documentation, without inventing continuous brake torque. Wheel brake mounting, stop distances and wet-floor traction remain open. [OEM stop/brake procedure](https://docs.universal-robots.com/tutorials/controlling-robot-externally/stop-recovery.html).

No preparation total is reported. Local passing-path times use conservative all-point bounds at 20 mm/s working, 50 mm/s transfer and 0.25 rad/s joints; cart speed is 0.10 m/s. The inherited P16 estimate is 2,823.529 seconds per root with duty allowance, not a measured peeling cycle. The P16's 150 N at 3.4 mm/s, 200 mm travel, 4 N side-load limit and 20% duty still require a separate guide. Greens soak and potato rinse/drain allowances remain in the schedule, but missing connections and station times prevent summing a meal. [P16](https://www.actuonix.com/assets/images/datasheets/ActuonixP16Datasheet.pdf), [schedule](../../sim/r09/integrator/results/schedule.json).

The cost ledger has one reserve and one safety package: CNY {cost['subtotal_cny']:,.0f} subtotal + {cost['reserve_cny']:,.0f} reserve = **{cost['total_cny']:,.0f}**. Most component prices are unquoted China planning allowances, visibly marked; current supplier quotes were not obtained. [Costs](../../sim/r09/integrator/results/costs.csv).

**Renders and delivery boundary.** [Overview](../../sim/r09/integrator/renders/overview.png), [conditional parked snapshot](../../sim/r09/integrator/renders/parked.png), [stations](../../sim/r09/integrator/renders/stations.png), [24-frame strip](../../sim/r09/integrator/renders/carrot_local_strip.png). All are CPU geometry renders at ≤1600 px. The strip shows the saved local mandoline path only, explicitly labelled as not an executed carrot sequence. A genuine end-to-end execution strip cannot be supplied because no such sequence exists.

The next structural work is to define physical food end-cradles and peeler access, a supported/detachable tray interface and a consistent station ownership controller, then qualify the cheaper arm and tether/brake integration. Adding a tall lift has no demonstrated benefit here. Finite search, clear statics and a legal parking snapshot are insufficient for an integrated prototype release.
'''
 (ROOT/'posts/r09/integrator.md').write_text(text,encoding='utf-8')
 print('Chinese summary and English engineering post written')
